 "_doc": "Key-level ownership of localization keys (PLAN R.4 for the base files, addendum 3.7 / RV-P8 for the feature files). Resolution (LocalizationManager.owner_of, tools/loc/csv_lint.py, F1 validator K8): an `exact` entry wins; else ITEM_<id>[_DESC|_HINT] of the item ids of the Lua files named in `item_files`; else the LONGEST matching `prefix`. A key that no file claims is unconstrained (it only has to be unique). A non-legacy file may define only keys it owns; da.csv (legacy base) and zz_final.csv (copy-pass overrides of NON-voiced keys) are exempt. `owner` is the package that edits the file. A new CSV gets its key families here by a change request to P03 (new_csv.py creates the file and its keep-import but never edits this table).",
