 "notes": [
  "INDRET_ONLY_HOME is an exact key of features_ui.csv (P06 needs it in wave 4); it wins over F7's INDRET_ prefix.",
  "HYGGE_LABEL / HYGGE_SCORE_FMT are exact keys of features_ui.csv; they win over home.csv's HYGGE_ prefix.",
  "PERK_SPEED|ENERGY|LUCK|DISCOUNT are exact keys of finds.csv; F8's per-line formats are PERKLINE_<KIND>_FMT (no clash).",
  "F7 and F8 may NOT use HOME_UI_ or WARDROBE_UI_ (features_ui.csv) - their screen strings use HUSBYG_/KISTE_ and GARDEROBE_/SLOTCELL_/PERKLINE_.",
  "P13 must not define QUEST_*/OBJ_* keys of bogtraeet, moonstone_crown, snurresvampen or slotsdroemmen (features_quests.csv owns them, incl. the dialogue choice and reminder lines QUEST_<ID>_CHOICE / _REMIND).",
  "Base files (core ... forest) follow PLAN R.4. Where the table says `UI_*`, `HUD_*` or `DIALOGUE_*` with a qualifier (new / shared / hints) only the named keys and the named sub-families (UI_WEEKDAY_, UI_MONTH_) are claimed: other packages (P04 UI_SLEEP, P11 UI_READ, P14 DIALOGUE_CHOICE_*, P17 hud strings) keep their own keys without a collision.",
  "P12 owns every ITEM_/RECIPE_/SHOP_ key that no more specific entry claims; P20 owns ITEM_BABY_* and the ten species keys; the feature CSVs (F1) own the ITEM_<id> keys of furniture.lua, clothing.lua and building_materials.lua."
 ]
}
